bug_report:
musttail vs noreturn discovery
Take:
```
[[gnu::noreturn]]
extern void x();

[[gnu::noinline]]
static int f(int)
{
  x();
  return 0;
}

int g(int);
int h(int t)
{
  if (t == 1)
  [[clang::musttail]]
    return f(1);
  [[clang::musttail]]
  return g(t);
}

```

This fails with GCC and not clang because GCC discovers that x is noreturn and then rejects the tail call.

Note this might be or might not be part ofPR 119376, I have not checked fully yet.
